# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"A quantum-classical workflow runs as one managed workflow job. Its classical stages run on your compute profile, and the primitive jobs that it sends to an IBM Quantum&reg; QPU run on your instance and count against your usage. From that one job, you can report each stage, find the QPU jobs, and cancel them. To start a job and check its status and logs, see [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow).\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Un workflow quantique-classique s'exécute comme un seul job de workflow géré. Ses étapes classiques s'exécutent sur ton profil de calcul, et les jobs de primitives qu'il envoie à un QPU IBM Quantum&reg; s'exécutent sur ton instance et comptent dans ton utilisation. À partir de ce job unique, tu peux signaler chaque étape, trouver les jobs QPU et les annuler. Pour lancer un job et vérifier son statut et ses journaux, consulte [Exécuter un workflow géré](/guides/run-managed-workflow).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before you begin, [deploy your first managed workflow](/guides/deploy-first-managed-workflow).\n"
msgstr "Avant de commencer, [déploie ton premier workflow géré](/guides/deploy-first-managed-workflow).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create the Runtime service {#create-the-runtime-service}"
msgstr "Créer le service Runtime {#create-the-runtime-service}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create the Runtime service in your workflow code with `get_runtime_service()`, and use it in the same way that you use `QiskitRuntimeService` locally. The following workflow runs a Bell circuit with the Sampler primitive, reports each stage with `update_status()`, and returns the counts:\n"
msgstr "Crée le service Runtime dans le code de ton workflow avec `get_runtime_service()`, et utilise-le de la même manière que tu utilises `QiskitRuntimeService` en local. Le workflow suivant exécute un circuit de Bell avec la primitive Sampler, signale chaque étape avec `update_status()` et renvoie les comptages :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`get_runtime_service()` returns a `QiskitRuntimeService` that is set up for your managed workflow job, and it provides the following:\n"
msgstr "`get_runtime_service()` renvoie un `QiskitRuntimeService` configuré pour ton job de workflow géré, et il fournit ce qui suit :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Credentials.** The Runtime service uses the API key, instance, and channel that you used to call `run()`, so the workflow code needs no credentials.\n"
msgstr "**Identifiants.** Le service Runtime utilise la clé API, l'instance et le canal que tu as utilisés pour appeler `run()`, de sorte que le code du workflow n'a besoin d'aucun identifiant.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Tracking.** A workflow records every primitive job that runs through this Runtime service under the managed workflow job, including Sampler, Estimator, and Executor jobs, and jobs in a session or batch. You can list them with `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"
msgstr "**Suivi.** Un workflow enregistre chaque job de primitive exécuté via ce service Runtime sous le job de workflow géré, y compris les jobs Sampler, Estimator et Executor, ainsi que les jobs dans une session ou un batch. Tu peux les lister avec `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Cancellation.** When you call `job.cancel()`, the managed workflow also cancels the workflow's sessions, batches, and primitive jobs that are still running.\n"
msgstr "**Annulation.** Lorsque tu appelles `job.cancel()`, le workflow géré annule aussi les sessions, les batches et les jobs de primitives du workflow qui sont encore en cours d'exécution.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow does not track or cancel the jobs of a service that you create with `QiskitRuntimeService()`, although the jobs still run. If the workflow must use another service, cancel its jobs in a [`SIGTERM` handler](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled).\n"
msgstr "Un workflow géré ne suit pas et n'annule pas les jobs d'un service que tu crées avec `QiskitRuntimeService()`, bien que les jobs s'exécutent quand même. Si le workflow doit utiliser un autre service, annule ses jobs dans un [gestionnaire `SIGTERM`](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run primitives in a session or batch {#run-primitives-in-a-session-or-batch}"
msgstr "Exécuter des primitives dans une session ou un batch {#run-primitives-in-a-session-or-batch}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow also tracks primitive jobs that run in a session or batch. Create the session or batch from a backend that the Runtime service returned, and create the primitives inside the `with` block. `Session` works in the same way:\n"
msgstr "Un workflow géré suit aussi les jobs de primitives qui s'exécutent dans une session ou un batch. Crée la session ou le batch à partir d'un backend renvoyé par le service Runtime, et crée les primitives à l'intérieur du bloc `with`. `Session` fonctionne de la même manière :\n"

