#, no-wrap
msgid "The `job` object exists only in the notebook that started the run. In a new notebook, get the job again with `client.job(\"<your-job-id>\")`, then call `runtime_jobs()` on it. See [Find a job from a new session](/guides/run-managed-workflow#find-a-job-from-a-new-session).\n"
msgstr "L'objet `job` n'existe que dans le notebook qui a lancé l'exécution. Dans un nouveau notebook, récupère de nouveau le job avec `client.job(\"<your-job-id>\")`, puis appelle `runtime_jobs()` dessus. Consulte [Retrouver un job depuis une nouvelle session](/guides/run-managed-workflow#find-a-job-from-a-new-session).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the QPU usage and run times of each QPU job, see [View job metrics](/guides/monitor-job#view-job-metrics). For the usage of your whole instance in the current period, call `client.usage()`. To see how long each stage of the managed workflow job took, see [Check how long each stage took](/guides/run-managed-workflow#check-how-long-each-stage-took).\n"
msgstr "Pour l'utilisation du QPU et les temps d'exécution de chaque job QPU, consulte [Afficher les métriques d'un job](/guides/monitor-job#view-job-metrics). Pour l'utilisation de l'ensemble de ton instance sur la période en cours, appelle `client.usage()`. Pour voir combien de temps a pris chaque étape du job de workflow géré, consulte [Vérifier la durée de chaque étape](/guides/run-managed-workflow#check-how-long-each-stage-took).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cancel linked QPU jobs {#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs}"
msgstr "Annuler les jobs QPU liés {#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you cancel a managed workflow job with `job.cancel()`, the workflow also tries to cancel the QPU work that the workflow started:\n"
msgstr "Lorsque tu annules un job de workflow géré avec `job.cancel()`, le workflow essaie aussi d'annuler le travail QPU qu'il a lancé :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Sessions and batches.** The workflow cancels each of the workflow's sessions and batches, which also cancels their queued jobs.\n"
msgstr "**Sessions et batches.** Le workflow annule chacune de ses sessions et chacun de ses batches, ce qui annule aussi leurs jobs en file d'attente.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Other primitive jobs.** The workflow cancels each of the workflow's other primitive jobs that are still queued or running.\n"
msgstr "**Autres jobs de primitives.** Le workflow annule chacun de ses autres jobs de primitives qui sont encore en file d'attente ou en cours d'exécution.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.cancel()` returns a message for each QPU job and session, so you can check what was canceled:\n"
msgstr "`job.cancel()` renvoie un message pour chaque job QPU et chaque session, ce qui te permet de vérifier ce qui a été annulé :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a workflow that ran in a batch, the message looks like the following:\n"
msgstr "Pour un workflow exécuté dans un batch, le message ressemble à ce qui suit :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the client cannot create a `QiskitRuntimeService` from your local credentials, it cancels only the managed workflow job. Cancel the QPU jobs yourself with their IDs from `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"
msgstr "Si le client ne peut pas créer un `QiskitRuntimeService` à partir de tes identifiants locaux, il n'annule que le job de workflow géré. Annule toi-même les jobs QPU avec leurs ID obtenus via `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When a workflow stops a job itself, for example because it reached the 24-hour limit, it does not cancel its QPU jobs. Cancel them with their IDs from `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"
msgstr "Lorsqu'un workflow arrête lui-même un job, par exemple parce qu'il a atteint la limite de 24 heures, il n'annule pas ses jobs QPU. Annule-les avec leurs ID obtenus via `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: the scheduler's timeout and blocked-account stops (update_fleets_jobs_statuses.py stop_job_if_timeout, FleetsJobCanceller) cancel only the fleet. Only the user stop endpoint (StopJobUseCase) cancels runtime jobs. Confirm whether this is intended before publishing. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshoot QPU jobs in a workflow {#troubleshoot-qpu-jobs-in-a-workflow}"
msgstr "Dépanner les jobs QPU dans un workflow {#troubleshoot-qpu-jobs-in-a-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Problem | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `get_runtime_service()` raises `KeyError: 'QISKIT_IBM_CHANNEL'`. | The code runs in your local notebook, not in a managed workflow job. Use `QiskitRuntimeService()` locally. |\n"
"| `update_status()` returns `False`, and the logs show `'sub_status' not provided or is not valid`. | The value is not one of the `Job` constants, or the job is no longer active. |\n"
"| `job.runtime_jobs()` returns `[]`. | The workflow created its service with `QiskitRuntimeService()`, or it has not run a primitive yet. |\n"
"| A session's jobs are not tracked. | The session was created from a backend of a different service. Get the backend from `get_runtime_service()`. |\n"
"| The workflow logs show `Could not associate runtime job with serverless job`. | The workflow could not record a primitive job. The primitive job still runs, but it is not tracked. |\n"
"| `job.cancel()` shows `No QiskitRuntimeService can be associated to the given token and instance.` | The client could not create a `QiskitRuntimeService` from your local credentials, so it canceled only the managed workflow job. |\n"
"| `client.job()` fails with `Job [...] not found`. | The job ID is wrong, or the job belongs to another user. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Problème | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `get_runtime_service()` lève `KeyError: 'QISKIT_IBM_CHANNEL'`. | Le code s'exécute dans ton notebook local, et non dans un job de workflow géré. Utilise `QiskitRuntimeService()` en local. |\n"
"| `update_status()` renvoie `False`, et les journaux affichent `'sub_status' not provided or is not valid`. | La valeur n'est pas l'une des constantes `Job`, ou le job n'est plus actif. |\n"
"| `job.runtime_jobs()` renvoie `[]`. | Le workflow a créé son service avec `QiskitRuntimeService()`, ou il n'a pas encore exécuté de primitive. |\n"
"| Les jobs d'une session ne sont pas suivis. | La session a été créée à partir d'un backend d'un autre service. Obtiens le backend avec `get_runtime_service()`. |\n"
"| Les journaux du workflow affichent `Could not associate runtime job with serverless job`. | Le workflow n'a pas pu enregistrer un job de primitive. Le job de primitive s'exécute quand même, mais il n'est pas suivi. |\n"
"| `job.cancel()` affiche `No QiskitRuntimeService can be associated to the given token and instance.` | Le client n'a pas pu créer un `QiskitRuntimeService` à partir de tes identifiants locaux ; il n'a donc annulé que le job de workflow géré. |\n"
"| `client.job()` échoue avec `Job [...] not found`. | L'ID du job est incorrect, ou le job appartient à un autre utilisateur. |\n"

